{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>Behold, I have given a thousand pieces of silver to your brother.</b> He said this concerning what he mentioned above — sheep and cattle and servants and maidservants — which were worth a thousand pieces of silver. 'To your brother' — to the one you said is your brother. And this silver is for you a covering of eyes (כסות עינים), to cover the eyes of all who look at you, since I gave it to your brother and not to you — for had I given it to you, everyone would have been murmuring and saying, 'See what he gave her as her hire!' But now that I gave it to your brother, they will say: the king needed to ransom himself and gave money against his will, and besides, he hates Abraham and desires his death. And this matter will be for you an answer (פ״פ) to all the people who are with you, and with all who come into the world you will be able to argue and justify yourself." "<b>And there are those</b> who interpreted <b>'and with all, and you shall be rebuked' (ואת כל ונוכחת)</b>: nevertheless Sarah rebuked him and did not wish to forgive him for the insult of the seizure, and all this was because of the great humility that was hers. Or, <b>'and with all' (ואת כל)</b> may be joined to what precedes it: 'לכל אשר אתך ואת כל' — and 'ונוכחת' means: it is fitting for you that from this time you be present (נוכחת). And the opinion of our Rabbis, of blessed memory, is that כסות עינים is a curse that was fulfilled in her seed, and from here the Rabbis derived: do not take lightly the curse of an ordinary person in your eyes." "<b>And there are those</b> who further interpreted: behold, it is so that you should say 'he is my brother' — a covering of eyes (כסות עינים) and a way of discipline — to whom? 'To all who are with you,' that is, to the members of your household; but 'with all the world, ונוכחת' — you shall be present, that is, you shall not say thus, for it is possible that you may come to a stumbling block." "<b>And in the Midrash:</b> כסות עינים — they made her a covering (כסות) so that everyone would gaze at her beauty and not at her ugliness (ולא בנויה). Another interpretation: כסות עינים — she is made of eyes, eyes (עינים עינים)."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {1 "פ״פ left untranslated in the body as it appears to be an abbreviation; its expansion is uncertain — possibly פה פה ('an answer here') or similar. The translation reflects the contextual sense without resolving the abbreviation."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:13:58.022004570Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}